  "summary": "Claire Lomas, a 44-year-old charity campaigner who became known for completing major races in a bionic suit after being paralysed in a 2007 horse-riding accident, has died following an accident in Jordan on 22 August. She raised nearly £1m through events nationwide, famously finished the 2012 London Marathon over 17 days, lit the Paralympic cauldron in Trafalgar Square later that year, and completed the Great North Run in 2016 while pregnant—taking five days—after being denied a place in the Vitality London 10k. Her family asked for privacy as they grieve."
}
